glibc: find libraries and data directories relative to the loaded ld.so/libc.so

The dynamic linker resolves its own path at startup (PT_INTERP or argv[0],
symlinks followed) and searches that directory instead of the configured
system directories, so DT_NEEDED without a RUNPATH and libc's own
dlopens (NSS, libresolv, libgcc_s) find the libraries installed next to
it wherever the installation was copied.

gconv modules, locales, the locale archive, message catalogs and zoneinfo
are looked up under the prefix libc.so.6 was loaded from (dladdr, two
levels up) instead of the configured one, so its bytes do not depend on
where it was built for. Environment overrides and paths outside $(prefix)
are unchanged. The static libc has no libc.so to anchor on and gets no
default directories rather than the configured prefix, which may not
exist at run time and could be planted.

Signed-off-by: Jörg Thalheim <joerg@thalheim.io>
